            "format": "tikz",
            "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 17 p17-q1d-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (T) at (-0.65,1.352);\\coordinate (B) at (-0.65,-1.352);\\coordinate (E) at (-0.65,0);\\coordinate (L) at (-1.5,0);\\coordinate (R) at (1.5,0);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (0,0) circle (1.5) (T)--(B) (L)--(R);\n\\path (T)--(E) node[midway,right] {$6$};\\path (E)--(B) node[midway,right] {$6$};\\path (L)--(E) node[midway,above] {$x$};\\path (E)--(R) node[midway,above] {$x+5$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
            "src": null,
            "widthMm": 41.5,
            "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
            "overlayOf": null,
            "transparent": false,
            "axes": null,
            "spec": {
              "sourcePage": 17,
              "sourceRegion": "Question 1(d)",
              "description": "Intersecting chords with unequal horizontal segments; no perpendicular marker is printed or added.",
              "mathematics": "Vertical segments 6 and 6; horizontal segments x and x+5.",
              "answerVisibility": "Unknown labels are retained without supplied answers."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=4$",
          "worked": "By the Power of a Point Theorem,\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x+5)&=6\\times6\\\\x^2+5x&=36\\\\x^2+5x-36&=0\\\\(x+9)(x-4)&=0\\\\x&=4.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $x=-9$ since a length is positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
